# `project *, x = ...`: DS0117 pointing to `extend`; the columns after it are still parsed.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | project *, double = amount * 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..46
  PIPELINE@0..45
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    PROJECT_OP@15..45
      IDENT@15..22 "project"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      ERROR@23..25
        STAR@23..24 "*"
        COMMA@24..25 ","
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@26..45
        NAME@26..32
          IDENT@26..32 "double"
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        EQ@33..34 "="
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        BIN_EXPR@35..45
          NAME_REF@35..41
            IDENT@35..41 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
          STAR@42..43 "*"
          WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
          LITERAL@44..45
            LONG@44..45 "2"
  WHITESPACE@45..46 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `project *` is SQL's `SELECT *`
  --> query:1:24
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | project *, double = amount * 2
  |                        ^ `project` lists the columns to keep
  |
  = help: to keep every column and add computed ones, use `extend`: `extend double = amount * 2`
